    "lawCode": "Amd §§27-2701, 27-2703, 27-2705, 27-2707, 27-2709 & 27-2713, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5817A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the environmental conservation law, in\nrelation to the recycling of film plastic\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo help support the New York City-wide recycling program state wide to\naccept film plastic in their collection bins.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis bill amends provisions of the \"Plastic Bag Reduction, Reuse and\nRecycling Act\" (the \"Act\"), which was enacted by the State in 2008.\nSpecifically, the bill would require stores state wide to accept film\nplastic in their collection bins. Subdivision 2 of Section 27-2701 of\nthe environmental conservation law is amended by adding film plastic\nto the definition of \"manufacturer.\" Section 27-2701 is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 7 defining film plastic. Article 27, Title 27\nof the environmental conservation law is amended throughout to include\nfilm plastic in the plastic bag recycling program.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nNew York City's \"Plastic Carryout Bag and Film Plastic Recycling Law,\"\nsigned into law in 2008, differed from the State's \"Plastic Bad\nReduction, Reuse and Recycling Act\" because it imposed stricter\nplastic bag collection requirements on a larger number of stores, and\napplied to film plastic as well as to plastic carryout bags. The\nchanges proposed in this bill would align state law with the City's\npreempted stricter standard by adding film plastic to the plastic bag\nrecycling program that is already in place statewide.\n\nThese changes will lead to greater compliance with the recycling\nprogram by both retail stores and by consumers, who will have greater\nopportunities to recycle their unwanted plastic bags and film plastic.\nAs indicated in the approval memo of the New York State \"Plastic Bag\nReduction, Reuse and Recycling Act\", these changes to the bill will\nhelp support the successful City-wide recycling program that was in\nplace before the State Act took effect.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:.\n\n2012: A10433 (Kavanagh) Environmental Conservation\n\nFISCAL IMPACT ON THE STATE:\n\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect on March 1, 2015.\n\n",
